    {
      "id": "scene_OJ_PMZaFKx",
      "stageId": "ALVWX7b4Lx",
      "type": "quiz",
      "title": "Quiz: Document Structure",
      "order": 4,
      "content": {
        "type": "quiz",
        "questions": [
          {
            "id": "q1",
            "type": "single",
            "question": "Which of the following lists the tags in the correct order for a minimal HTML5 page?",
            "options": [
              {
                "value": "A",
                "label": "<!DOCTYPE html> <html> <head> <title>Page Title</title> </head> <body> </body> </html>"
              },
              {
                "value": "B",
                "label": "<html> <head> <title>Page Title</title> </head> <body> </body> </html>"
              },
              {
                "value": "C",
                "label": "<!DOCTYPE html> <head> <title>Page Title</title> </head> <body> </body>"
              },
              {
                "value": "D",
                "label": "<!DOCTYPE html> <html> <body> <head> <title>Page Title</title> </head> </body> </html>"
              }
            ],
            "answer": [
              "A"
            ],
            "analysis": "Option A includes the required doctype declaration, html root, head with a title element, and body. The other options are missing the doctype, have tags in the wrong order, or place the head inside the body.",
            "points": 5,
            "hasAnswer": true
          },
          {
            "id": "q2",
            "type": "multiple",
            "question": "Select all statements that correctly describe the element that holds the page title in an HTML document (choose all that apply).",
            "options": [
              {
                "value": "A",
                "label": "It is placed inside the <head> element."
              },
              {
                "value": "B",
                "label": "Its content is displayed in the browser's title bar or tab."
              },
              {
                "value": "C",
                "label": "It can appear multiple times in a single HTML document."
              },
              {
                "value": "D",
                "label": "It is defined with the <title> tag."
              }
            ],
            "answer": [
              "A",
              "B",
              "D"
            ],
            "analysis": "The page title is set with the <title> tag, which must be inside the <head> section, and its text appears in the browser’s title bar or tab. An HTML document may have only one <title> element, so option C is incorrect.",
            "points": 5,
            "hasAnswer": true
          }
        ]
      },
      "actions": [
        {
          "id": "action_Er2ZN1P3",
          "type": "speech",
          "text": "Now let's check what we've learned about the basic HTML skeleton. You'll see two questions—one about the correct tag order for a minimal page, and another about the element that holds the page title."
        },
        {
          "id": "action_Fl4fvoHl",
          "type": "speech",
          "text": "For a minimal HTML5 document you need three things in this exact order: the <!DOCTYPE html> declaration, the <html> root element, and inside it a <head> section followed by a <body>. The <title> tag belongs in the <head>. Option A follows that structure perfectly, while the other choices either miss the doctype, place the <head> after the <body>, or omit required tags."
        },
        {
          "id": "action_zcvrWJ0C",
          "type": "speech",
          "text": "The page title is defined with the <title> tag, and it must appear once inside the <head>. Its text shows up in the browser’s title bar or tab, but it never appears inside the page content itself. So statements A, B, and D are correct; the title element should not be repeated, making statement C false."
        },
        {
          "id": "action_LDF_WcCg",
          "type": "discussion",
          "topic": "Why is the correct order of HTML tags important for browsers and developers?",
          "prompt": "Think about how a browser reads the document and how it affects what you see on the page.",
          "agentId": "gen-server-3"
        }
      ],
      "createdAt": 1777564351048,
      "updatedAt": 1777564351048
    },
    {
      "id": "scene_Hv8sl-OpNG",
