      "content": {
        "type": "slide",
        "canvas": {
          "id": "RNOd_IJLPTGzZse5xQE-4",
          "viewportSize": 1000,
          "viewportRatio": 0.5625,
          "theme": {
            "backgroundColor": "#ffffff",
            "themeColors": [
              "#5b9bd5",
              "#ed7d31",
              "#a5a5a5",
              "#ffc000",
              "#4472c4"
            ],
            "fontColor": "#333333",
            "fontName": "Microsoft YaHei",
            "outline": {
              "color": "#d14424",
              "width": 2,
              "style": "solid"
            },
            "shadow": {
              "h": 0,
              "v": 0,
              "blur": 10,
              "color": "#000000"
            }
          },
          "elements": [
            {
              "id": "text_4oMRJyoo",
              "type": "text",
              "left": 60,
              "top": 60,
              "width": 880,
              "height": 70,
              "content": "<p style=\"font-size:32px; font-weight:bold; text-align:center;\">Headings and Paragraphs</p>",
              "defaultFontName": "Microsoft YaHei",
              "defaultColor": "#333333",
              "rotate": 0
            },
            {
              "id": "text_46yNxPUn",
              "type": "text",
              "left": 60,
              "top": 150,
              "width": 880,
              "height": 103,
              "content": "<p style=\"font-size:18px;\">• <strong>&lt;h1&gt;–&lt;h6&gt;</strong> define heading levels; <strong>&lt;h1&gt;</strong> is highest</p><p style=\"font-size:18px;\">• <strong>&lt;p&gt;</strong> creates a paragraph of text</p><p style=\"font-size:18px;\">• Use one <strong>&lt;h1&gt;</strong> per page for the main title</p>",
              "defaultFontName": "Microsoft YaHei",
              "defaultColor": "#333333",
              "rotate": 0
            },
            {
              "id": "text_3CpMRVku",
              "type": "text",
              "left": 80,
              "top": 280,
              "width": 840,
              "height": 94,
              "content": "<p style=\"font-size:16px; font-family:monospace; background:#f5f5f5; padding:8px;\">&lt;h1&gt;Main Title&lt;/h1&gt;<br/>&lt;h2&gt;Section Heading&lt;/h2&gt;<br/>&lt;p&gt;This is a paragraph.&lt;/p&gt;</p>",
              "defaultFontName": "Microsoft YaHei",
              "defaultColor": "#333333",
              "rotate": 0
            }
          ],
          "background": {
            "type": "solid",
            "color": "#ffffff"
          }
        }
      },
      "actions": [
        {
          "id": "action_6NDbPmQ9",
          "type": "spotlight",
          "elementId": "text_4oMRJyoo"
        },
        {
          "id": "action_rntsdJjg",
          "type": "speech",
          "text": "Okay, let's start with the big picture: this slide is all about headings and paragraphs in HTML."
        },
        {
          "id": "action_6p2ODpf6",
          "type": "spotlight",
          "elementId": "text_46yNxPUn"
        },
        {
          "id": "action_nP48AESp",
          "type": "speech",
          "text": "Here you can see the key points: <h1> through <h6> define six heading levels, with <h1> being the most important, and the <p> tag creates a paragraph of text."
        },
        {
          "id": "action_37CM82AY",
          "type": "laser",
          "elementId": "text_46yNxPUn"
        },
        {
          "id": "action_tO3eNt40",
          "type": "speech",
          "text": "Remember, it's a good practice to use only one <h1> per page for the main title, and then use the lower‑level headings to structure your content."
        },
        {
          "id": "action_weXyB6ze",
          "type": "spotlight",
          "elementId": "text_3CpMRVku"
        },
        {
          "id": "action_4iteh6oz",
          "type": "speech",
          "text": "Now, let's look at the example code. This snippet shows an <h1> for the main title, an <h2> for a section heading, and a <p> that holds a paragraph of text."
        },
        {
          "id": "action_iKqkxoxS",
          "type": "laser",
          "elementId": "text_3CpMRVku"
        },
        {
          "id": "action_hx-GIerG",
          "type": "speech",
          "text": "Try typing this into your own HTML file and see how the browser renders each heading size and the paragraph spacing."
        },
        {
          "id": "action_1SQPpApu",
          "type": "speech",
          "text": "Great job! You've just learned how to structure headings and paragraphs, a foundational step for building clear, accessible web pages."
        }
      ],
      "createdAt": 1777564393404,
      "updatedAt": 1777564393404
    },
    {
      "id": "scene_iop5hNnNJF",
      "stageId": "ALVWX7b4Lx",
      "type": "quiz",
      "title": "Quiz: Headings & Paragraphs",
      "order": 6,
      "content": {
        "type": "quiz",
        "questions": [
          {
            "id": "q1",
            "type": "single",
            "question": "Which HTML heading tag should be used for a sub‑section within an article that already has a main heading using <h1>?",
            "options": [
              {
                "value": "A",
                "label": "<h2>"
              },
              {
                "value": "B",
                "label": "<h3>"
              },
              {
                "value": "C",
                "label": "<h4>"
              },
              {
                "value": "D",
                "label": "<h5>"
              }
            ],
            "answer": [
              "A"
            ],
            "analysis": "The main title uses <h1>. The next level of hierarchy is a sub‑section, which is correctly marked with <h2>. <h3> and lower headings are for deeper nesting.",
            "points": 5,
            "hasAnswer": true
          },
          {
            "id": "q2",
            "type": "single",
            "question": "Which HTML tag creates a paragraph of text?",
            "options": [
              {
                "value": "A",
                "label": "<div>"
              },
              {
                "value": "B",
                "label": "<p>"
              },
              {
                "value": "C",
                "label": "<span>"
              },
              {
                "value": "D",
                "label": "<section>"
              }
            ],
            "answer": [
              "B"
            ],
            "analysis": "<p> is the semantic element specifically designed to contain a paragraph of text. The other tags serve different structural or inline purposes.",
            "points": 5,
            "hasAnswer": true
          }
        ]
      },
      "actions": [
        {
          "id": "action_52OIw-jo",
          "type": "speech",
          "text": "Alright, let's see how well you've grasped the basics we just covered about headings and paragraphs. You'll have two quick questions—just pick the best answer for each."
        },
        {
          "id": "action_dgyt22xq",
          "type": "speech",
          "text": "Remember, heading tags follow a logical hierarchy. Since the main title of the article uses <h1>, the next level down for a sub‑section is <h2>. That's the tag that tells browsers and screen readers, \"Hey, this is a subsection of the main heading.\""
        },
        {
          "id": "action_gigZtixj",
          "type": "speech",
          "text": "And when you want to write regular blocks of text, the proper semantic tag is <p>. It automatically adds spacing and tells browsers this is a paragraph, unlike <div> or <span> which are generic containers."
        },
        {
          "id": "action_6HhDG2mq",
          "type": "discussion",
          "topic": "Why is it important to use the correct heading levels and paragraph tags in HTML?",
          "prompt": "Think about accessibility, SEO, and how browsers render the page.",
          "agentId": "gen-server-3"
        }
      ],
      "createdAt": 1777564424536,
      "updatedAt": 1777564424536
    },
    {
